{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01UTkoPnLbE72dezQBrEjH8a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-user, single-folder productivity + R&D control system for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (no syncing, no database â€” markdown files are the source of truth).\n\n- **What it is:** A self-contained Python-stdlib web app (`anchor_gui.py`) that runs as a persistent background Windows service (NSSM service `anchor`, bound to `http://localhost:8777`) and serves a browser dashboard generated fresh on every request. A CLI mirror (`anchor.py`) provides the same logic plus static `dashboard.html` generation.\n\n- **Core purpose (task management):** Capture and move personal/work tasks through a lifecycle (Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled / Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored) across life domains (academic, commercial, family, writing). It reads/writes plain markdown (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`) directly â€” no Cowork sandbox, no external deps.\n\n- **The bigger thing it ships (R&D Control Surface):** A \"Project Cockpit\" that turns each project's window into mission-control for the **trio** workflow â€” researchPrime (research) â†’ Crucible (planning) â†’ Foreman (build). Each lane shows its most-recent session as a tile with one honest status light; clicking expands an inline panel with a cached, grounded summary stacked over a real, resizable terminal.\n\n- **Terminal substrate it provides:** Real interactive **ConPTY** terminal sessions (via the one declared native exception, `pywinpty`), each isolated in its own git worktree+branch, registered durably under `.anchor/`, reachable over a hand-rolled stdlib WebSocket (+ SSE fallback) into xterm.js. A new session auto-loads the lane's skill **once**, greets **once** â€” fixing the old repeating-prompt bug.\n\n- **Supporting machinery it includes:** Validated/cached session & project summaries (generate-twice + grounding filter), per-lane doc-role maps, cost/tokens/time rollups, a Grass-Catchers idea board with promote-to-lane, type-aware deliverable launch (skill/tool/service/program/doc), runnable deliverable previews (hard-guarded never to bind `:8777`), stage handoffs between planâ†’build, and an engine toggle (Claude â†” Gemini, research-only for Gemini).\n\n- **Reliability it ships:** A daily 5 AM self-test (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) that parses every file, boots a throwaway server, and walks the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces fully stubbed (no live `claude`, never touching `:8777` or real data), writing dated health reports and surfacing a red dashboard banner on failure.\n\n- **Status:** The v4 \"Project Cockpit\" was built by Foreman (9 waves green, 637 tests passing) and merged to master; the current branch (`foreman/rnd-v4.1-cockpit`) is iterating on rendering the project window as the locked Paradigm-2 cockpit."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45330,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"57eb5196-ac85-4b75-9764-bd79ba76d5e9","uuid":"1017ec83-f9e8-4128-98e7-8f3fa60f2315","request_id":"req_011Cc1v3ayquVVnrv2G6p8Pz"}
